]

CAMERA VIEW (framing only). Call setCameraView({ projection, ...these }) AFTER all geometry is added. Keep the projection MECHANISM from PROJECTION TYPE above (orthographic / sheared-oblique / perspective). For perspective these params set the pose (azimuth/elevation/roll); for the two parallel projections pose is a standard default (see PROJECTION TYPE above), and these params set only roll and framing (heightFraction):
{
  "heightFraction": 0.72
}

NOTES: Use an orthographic camera in a standard isometric pose for the default view; OrbitControls with target at the origin, zoom enabled, no panning needed. Arrows: THREE.ArrowHelper or cylinder shaft + cone head with headLength ≈ 0.6, headWidth ≈ 0.28 so short and long arrows read consistently. Dashed boxes: LineSegments with LineDashedMaterial and computeLineDistances(). Axis ticks as small LineSegments batched into one geometry per axis. Labels as CSS2DObject/sprite HTML so they stay screen-facing and legible while orbiting; keep them offset so they never overlap arrowheads. Toggle should cross-fade (opacity 1→0.12) rather than delete the inactive arrow+box, so the shared line is still visible. Right-hand-rule steps: animate a small curved arc arrow (TorusGeometry partial) sweeping from u to v in the u–v plane, then grow the red arrow along its axis with a scale/clip animation.  Render order: axes first, dashed boxes at low opacity, arrows last with depthWrite true.

